{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1546490-alot-of-gifts-feel-underpowered","id":1546490,"title":"Alot of Gifts feel underpowered","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-29T12:40:31-08:00","id":1546490,"title":"Alot of Gifts feel underpowered","content":"Is it just me, or do alot Aptitude Gifts in the cire riulesfeel like Skill Tricks by another name? It feels like though you could make your Skill Tricks activate at a reduced momentum cost as a Talent for the same result. Sure the gifts in the books set in Adventure-era and before have more powerful gifts, but nothing in modern times and beyond are like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-29T15:04:02-08:00","id":1546492,"title":"","content":"The issue to me is that skill tricks are too powerful. They should be things regular people can do, balanced in level with specialties, not powerful stuff. To me it would be limited to a few effects only:<br /> - 1 enhancement in a general use of the skill<br /> - 1 scale in a very specific situation<br /> - reduce the cost of an specific stunt by 2<br /> - reduce the cost of a small range of complications by 2<br /> <br /> Now on Gifts, some gifts are pretty situational or niche, but if you get into that condition you are king.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered